        "isolation": {
          "source": "bubblewrap 0.13.0 bwrap.xml (the bundled locked build's own manual source, read 2026-10-23): --unshare-all, --unshare-user, --disable-userns (requires --unshare-user), --die-with-parent, --proc, --dev, --size + --tmpfs, --perms, --ro-bind, --ro-bind-try, --bind, --chdir. No --share-net: the network namespace stays empty and only the gateway socket leads out. No --new-session: the runner's detached spawn already starts a session without a controlling terminal, and the process group must reach the CLI so SIGINT ends the turn first. S3-5 lane.",
          "shell": "/bin/sh",
          "socketPath": "/run/deckent-egress.sock",
          "proxy": { "host": "127.0.0.1", "port": 18080, "env": ["HTTPS_PROXY", "HTTP_PROXY", "https_proxy", "http_proxy"], "clear": ["NO_PROXY", "no_proxy"] },
          "configVisible": [".claude.json", ".claude.json.backup", ".credentials.json", ".oauth_refresh.lock", ".oauth_refresh.lock.owner"],
          "configVisibleSource": "S3-5 lane 2026-10-23 from CLI 2.1.309 strings (no run): the CLI keeps its state file and login in the config dir, writes them through a sibling temporary file + rename and refreshes the login under a lock beside them. Every other existing entry of the login dir is masked (a directory becomes empty private memory, a file unreadable). Unmeasured against the real CLI until the lead's acceptance run.",
          "configMaxEntries": 4096,
          "refreshLock": { "names": [".oauth_refresh.lock", ".oauth_refresh.lock.owner"], "waitMs": 30000, "pollMs": 100, "staleMs": 600000,
            "source": "f5 lane 2026-10-24: names from configVisible (S3-5, CLI 2.1.309 strings); none exists at rest and none appeared during in-realm --version, --help and auth status (names-only watch of the login dir). The realm binds the login dir itself, so the CLI's lock file is the same inode for the realm and the person's own sessions; whether the CLI's stale-lock check uses a process id is unverified, and the realm's own PID namespace would break such a check both ways. Deckent therefore starts no spawn while a CLI lock name exists, and serializes its own spawns per login dir (staleMs: a holder older than this is stale even if its process id was reused)." },
          "limits": { "tmpfsBytes": 67108864, "fileSizeBlocks": 131072, "fileSizeBlocksSource": "POSIX ulimit -f counts 512-byte blocks (dash; bash in POSIX mode): 131072 blocks = 64 MiB, the largest file the isolated CLI may write", "openFiles": 1024,
            "cpuSeconds": 60, "cpuGraceSeconds": 5, "processes": 64, "dataBytes": 2147483648, "sampleMs": 50, "attributionPermille": 900,
            "exits": { "cpu-time": 201, "processes": 202, "memory": 203 },
            "boundsSource": "f5 lane 2026-10-24, measured in this realm with the real CLI 2.1.309 (Bun 1.4.4; --help and auth status only, no model call): peak RSS 180 MB, CPU 0.12 s, 8 realm tasks; RLIMIT_NPROC counts the realm's own user namespace on kernel 6.18 (7 runs auth status while the owner has hundreds of processes; 5 aborts), Bun sizes its reservations to RLIMIT_DATA (512 MiB runs --help; 256 MiB aborts); prlimit adds no measurable time (--help 98-104 ms either way). Per process: CPU soft 60 s (SIGXCPU) and hard +5 s (SIGKILL), data 2 GiB; realm: 64 tasks. Turn-time peaks unmeasured until the lead's real call.",
            "limiter": "/usr/bin/prlimit", "limiterSource": "prlimit(1) util-linux 2.39 --cpu=soft:hard, --nproc, --data (a single value sets soft and hard); setrlimit(2) man-pages 6.7: RLIMIT_CPU SIGXCPU at soft then SIGKILL at hard, RLIMIT_DATA covers brk and mmap since Linux 4.7, RLIMIT_NPROC counts threads (per user namespace since Linux 5.14 ucounts)" }
        }
